The '''Jean-Luc Island''' (also known as [[Mob Leader|Mob]] Island or [[Bandit]] Island) is an [[Locations|island]] located in the [[First Sea]]. 

==Usage==
The only purposes of the Jean-Luc Island is for the [[Saber/Puzzle|Saber Puzzle]], [[Chests|Diamond Chest]] and a [[Fruit Spawn Locations|fruit spawn location]]

==Location==
The Jean-Luc Island is located between the [[Magma Village]] and the [[Pirate Village]] islands in the [[First Sea]].

==Appearance==
The Jean-Luc Island is a small island that is very similar to the [[Cave Island]] in the [[Second Sea]], but smaller, unlike the Cave Island. There are some extra terrains and trees around the cave where the [[Mob Leader]] is located.

==Inhabitants==
The [[Mob Leader]] is the only inhabitant of the Jean-Luc Island.

==Chests==
The Jean-Luc Island has a [[Chests|Diamond Chest]], at the left of the [[Mob Leader]].

==Trivia==
* The Jean-Luc Island does not have an official name, the name "Jean-Luc" was given to it by [[User:Baguetteboing|Baguetteboing]], one of the Blox Fruits Wiki's bureaucrats.
* The Jean-Luc Island is one of the least visited islands in the [[First Sea]], as players only come here for the [[Saber/Puzzle|Saber Puzzle]] or to get the [[Bounty and Honor System|bounty/honor]] of the [[Mob Leader]], since his respawn time is low.
* The Jean-Luc Island does not have its own soundtrack, and instead uses the regular Sea soundtrack.
* Players cannot teleport to the Jean-Luc Island using [[Portal]]'s '''[C] World Warp''' ability.
* The Jean-Luc Island is the only island without any [[NPCs#Shop_NPCs|Shop NPCs]] but with [[Fruit Spawn Locations|fruit spawn points]].
* Driving a [[Miracle]] onto this island will make the [[Boats|boat]] land in the island, since this island is not considered an island, same happens in [[Remote Island]] and [[Cave Island]]. This can also happen on the base of [[Skylands]].

